-- title:
--   Theorem 5.1 — utility guarantee for private PADM: $\mathbb E\|\tilde u_{(k)}-u_\star\|_2^2\le\tilde\tau^k\|\tilde u_{(0)}-u_\star\|_2^2+\frac{1-\tilde\tau^k}{1-\tilde\tau}(\varsigma^2+\tau\varsigma)$
-- statement:
--   Let $(R,P_R)$ be a probability space of data records and $f:\mathbb R^p\times R\to\mathbb R$ a loss with $f(\cdot,d)$ convex for every $d$ and $f(x,\cdot)$ integrable for every $x$; let $F(x)=\mathbb E_{d\sim P_R}f(x,d)$, $g$ convex, $\beta>0$, and assume the proximal problems (13) for every $f(\cdot,d)$, for $F$ and for $g$ have minimizers. Write $T_{f(\cdot,d)}$ and $T_F$ for the PADM operators (15).
--
--   Assume:
--
--   1. **Condition 2:** for some $\mu\ge0$ and every $u\in\mathbb R^m$, $\ \mathbb E_{d\sim P_R}\|T_{f(\cdot,d)}(u)-T_F(u)\|_2^2\le\mu^2$;
--   2. $T_F$ is $\tau$-contractive, $\|T_F(u)-T_F(v)\|_2\le\tau\|u-v\|_2$, with $0<\tau<1$, and $u_\star$ is its (unique) fixed point;
--   3. the noise law $P_z$ on $\mathbb R^m$ has mean zero and second moment $\mathbb E\|z\|_2^2=\delta^2$, where
--   $$
--   \delta\in\Big(0,\ 2\sqrt{\tfrac{(1-\tau^2)^2}{\tau^2}-\mu^2}\Big)\neq\emptyset .
--   $$
--
--   Run private PADM (20), $\tilde u_{(0)}=A\tilde x_{(0)}$, $\tilde u_{(k)}=T_{f_k}(\tilde u_{(k-1)})+z_{(k)}/2$, with i.i.d. records $d_{(k)}\sim P_R$ and i.i.d. noises $z_{(k)}\sim P_z$ independent of the data. Then $\tilde\tau:=\tau^2+\tau\sqrt{\delta^2/4+\mu^2}<1$, and for every $k\in[n]$
--   $$
--   \mathbb E\big(\|\tilde u_{(k)}-u_\star\|_2^2\,\big|\,\Gamma_0\big)\le\tilde\tau^{\,k}\,\|\tilde u_{(0)}-u_\star\|_2^2+\frac{1-\tilde\tau^{\,k}}{1-\tilde\tau}\left(\frac{\delta^2}{4}+\mu^2+\tau\sqrt{\frac{\delta^2}{4}+\mu^2}\right). \tag{23}
--   $$
--
--   The first term is the linear convergence of noiseless PADM; the second is the stochastic error from the privacy noise and the sampling of the objective.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The expectation is over $P_R^{\otimes n}\otimes P_z^{\otimes n}$ on `(Fin n → R) × (Fin n → ℝᵐ)`. Condition 2 is stated with the integrability of the integrand, and $d\mapsto T_{f(\cdot,d)}(u)$ is assumed measurable for each $u$. The conclusion also states that $\|\tilde u_{(k)}-u_\star\|_2^2$ is integrable. $\tilde\tau$ is a variable bound by its defining equation.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: E[· | Γ₀] → plain expectation over P_R^{⊗n} ⊗ P_z^{⊗n}; reason: Γ₀ is generated by the deterministic ũ₍₀₎ = A x̃₍₀₎, so it is trivial
--   - encoding: T_F has a unique fixed point u⋆ → a point u⋆ with T_F(u⋆) = u⋆; reason: a τ-contraction with τ < 1 has at most one fixed point, so uniqueness is automatic; same instances
--   - encoding: Condition 2: E‖T_{f_k}(u) − T_F(u)‖₂² ≤ µ² → for every u, d ↦ ‖T_{f(·,d)}(u) − T_F(u)‖₂² is P_R-integrable with integral ≤ µ², and d ↦ T_{f(·,d)}(u) is measurable; reason: the expectation is finite in the source; the iterates are random variables (Definition 6); excludes only undefined cases
--   - encoding: noise with mean zero and E‖z(k)‖₂² = δ² → a probability measure P_z with ‖z‖₂² integrable, ∫ z dP_z = 0 and ∫ ‖z‖₂² dP_z = δ²; reason: the same assumptions, with finiteness of the second moment explicit
--   - encoding: the interval (0, 2√((1 − τ²)²/τ² − µ²)) is nonempty → hypothesis 0 < (1 − τ²)²/τ² − µ²; reason: the source's ≠ ∅ condition
--   - encoding: F(x) := E_{d∼P_R}[f(x, d)] → f(x, ·) measurable and P_R-integrable for every x; reason: needed for the expectation to be defined; excludes only undefined cases
--   - encoding: the sample proximal operators P_{β,f(·,d),A} used as everywhere defined → hypothesis that (13) for f(·,d) has a minimizer for every record d and input u; reason: Algorithm 1 is undefined otherwise; excludes only undefined cases
--   - encoding: P_{β,g,B} used as everywhere defined → hypothesis that (13) for g has a minimizer at every input; reason: T_{f_k} is undefined otherwise; excludes only undefined cases
--   - encoding: P_{β,F,A} used as everywhere defined → hypothesis that (13) for F has a minimizer at every input; reason: T_F is undefined otherwise; excludes only undefined cases
--   - generalization: the bound (23) → also concludes that ‖ũ₍ₖ₎ − u⋆‖₂² is integrable; reason: the proof establishes it; it rules out a junk integral
--   - generalization: full row rank of A and B (standing assumption, p.6) → not assumed; reason: the statement and its proof never use V or U; the source's case is an instance
-- source:
--   Li–Lai–Weng, Exact Feasibility and Privacy Amplification for Linearly Constrained Optimization, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 d58edbe0…0f3d), Theorem 5.1, p.11 (proof A.12, pp.27–28); Condition 2 and Definition 6, p.11; private PADM (20), p.8

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_padmIter
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_popLoss
import Definitions.Def_PADMPriv_IsContraction

namespace PADMPriv.Supplement

open MeasureTheory

/-- Theorem 5.1 (utility guarantee for private PADM) of Li–Lai–Weng, *Exact Feasibility and
Privacy Amplification for Linearly Constrained Optimization*, STOC 2027 submission manuscript
(sha256 d58edbe0…0f3d), p.11 (proof A.12, pp.27–28). Under Condition 2 (there is `µ ≥ 0` with
`E_{d∼P_R}‖T_{f(·,d)}(u) − T_F(u)‖₂² ≤ µ²` for every `u`), suppose `T_F` is `τ`-contractive with
`0 < τ < 1` and has a (unique) fixed point `u⋆`. If
`δ ∈ (0, 2√((1 − τ²)²/τ² − µ²)) ≠ ∅`, where `δ² = E‖z₍ₖ₎‖₂²` is the second moment of the
mean-zero noise, then `τ̃ := τ² + τ√(δ²/4 + µ²) < 1` and the iterates of private PADM satisfy, for
every `k ∈ [n]`,
`E[‖ũ₍ₖ₎ − u⋆‖₂² | Γ₀] ≤ τ̃ᵏ‖ũ₍₀₎ − u⋆‖₂² + (1 − τ̃ᵏ)/(1 − τ̃) · (δ²/4 + µ² + τ√(δ²/4 + µ²))` (23).

**Formalization Note** The records `d₍₁₎, …, d₍ₙ₎` are i.i.d. `P_R` and the noises i.i.d. `P_z`,
independent of the data (Section 3.3, p.8): the expectation is over
`P_R^{⊗n} ⊗ P_z^{⊗n}` on `(Fin n → R) × (Fin n → ℝᵐ)`, and `ũ₍ₖ₎ = PADMPriv.padmIter` (which adds
`z₍ₖ₎/2`, (20)) started at the deterministic `ũ₍₀₎ = A x̃₍₀₎`, so `E[· | Γ₀]` is a plain
expectation. `F = E_d f(·, d)` (`popLoss`) with `f(x, ·)` `P_R`-integrable. The noise law is a
probability measure with `‖z‖₂²` integrable, `∫ z dP_z = 0` and `∫ ‖z‖₂² dP_z = δ²`. Condition 2
is the integrability of `d ↦ ‖T_{f(·,d)}(u) − T_F(u)‖₂²` plus the bound; `d ↦ T_{f(·,d)}(u)` is
measurable for each `u` (the iterates are random variables, Definition 6). Standing assumptions
of Section 3: `f(·, d)`, `g` convex, `β > 0`, minimizers of (13) exist for `f(·, d)`, `F` and `g`, so
that every operator is defined. `τ̃` is a variable bound by its defining equation; the
conclusion also states the integrability of `‖ũ₍ₖ₎ − u⋆‖₂²`. -/
theorem theorem_5_1 {m p l n : ℕ} {R : Type*} [MeasurableSpace R]
    (A : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin p) ℝ) (B : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin l) ℝ) (c : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m))
    (PR : Measure R) [IsProbabilityMeasure PR]
    (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) → R → ℝ)
    (hfconv : ∀ d, ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ (fun x => f x d))
    (hfint : ∀ x, Integrable (fun d => f x d) PR)
    (g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin l) → ℝ) (hg : ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ g) (β : ℝ) (hβ : 0 < β)
    (hfprox : ∀ d u, ∃ x, IsProxMin β (fun x => f x d) A u x)
    (hFprox : ∀ u, ∃ x, IsProxMin β (popLoss f PR) A u x)
    (hgprox : ∀ v, ∃ y, IsProxMin β g B v y)
    (hTmeas : ∀ u, Measurable (fun d => padmOp β (fun x => f x d) g A B c u))
    (μ : ℝ) (hμ : 0 ≤ μ)
    (hcond2 : ∀ u : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m),
      Integrable (fun d => ‖padmOp β (fun x => f x d) g A B c u -
        padmOp β (popLoss f PR) g A B c u‖ ^ 2) PR ∧
      ∫ d, ‖padmOp β (fun x => f x d) g A B c u - padmOp β (popLoss f PR) g A B c u‖ ^ 2 ∂PR ≤
        μ ^ 2)
    (τ : ℝ) (hτ0 : 0 < τ) (hτ1 : τ < 1)
    (hcontr : IsContraction τ (padmOp β (popLoss f PR) g A B c))
    (ustar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) (hustar : padmOp β (popLoss f PR) g A B c ustar = ustar)
    (Pz : Measure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m))) [IsProbabilityMeasure Pz] (δ : ℝ)
    (hPzint : Integrable (fun z => ‖z‖ ^ 2) Pz) (hPzmean : ∫ z, z ∂Pz = 0)
    (hPzvar : ∫ z, ‖z‖ ^ 2 ∂Pz = δ ^ 2)
    (hne : 0 < (1 - τ ^ 2) ^ 2 / τ ^ 2 - μ ^ 2) (hδ0 : 0 < δ)
    (hδ1 : δ < 2 * Real.sqrt ((1 - τ ^ 2) ^ 2 / τ ^ 2 - μ ^ 2))
    (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)) (τt : ℝ)
    (hτt : τt = τ ^ 2 + τ * Real.sqrt (δ ^ 2 / 4 + μ ^ 2)) (k : ℕ) (hk1 : 1 ≤ k) (hkn : k ≤ n) :
    τt < 1 ∧
      Integrable (fun ω : (Fin n → R) × (Fin n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) =>
          ‖padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1 ω.2 k - ustar‖ ^ 2)
        ((Measure.pi fun _ : Fin n => PR).prod (Measure.pi fun _ : Fin n => Pz)) ∧
      ∫ ω, ‖padmIter β f g A B c x₀ ω.1 ω.2 k - ustar‖ ^ 2
          ∂((Measure.pi fun _ : Fin n => PR).prod (Measure.pi fun _ : Fin n => Pz)) ≤
        τt ^ k * ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin A x₀ - ustar‖ ^ 2 +
          (1 - τt ^ k) / (1 - τt) *
            (δ ^ 2 / 4 + μ ^ 2 + τ * Real.sqrt (δ ^ 2 / 4 + μ ^ 2)) := by sorry

end PADMPriv.Supplement
